    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7eb9571f921b73bffb63248f04a9f5debe22e586f987c5431ec273beea649f7b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the bulk terms, extending the x-contour enables an exact Gaussian integration that converts each term into a one-dimensional cubic phase with an explicit saddle. Extracting that saddle and deforming the remaining contours separates computable boundary pieces, while decay of the saddle-phase coefficients allows its infinite expansion to be truncated into a finite polynomial-phase sum whose bounded coefficient ranges can be addressed by precomputed grid values.",
