    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d27953bd0c77d06127847d133e7a9e241d094a127452825d4d531a2825b786dc",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The auxiliary lemmas close the cost proof as a staged certification pipeline: Euler-Maclaurin first replaces a cubic sum by an integral plus derivative corrections; recursive derivative bounds make the correction depth logarithmic; frequency splitting reduces those corrections to quadratic sums; nonstationary contour deformation supplies decay and truncation; saddle-aware branches reduce the remaining integrals to Airy-type or incomplete-Gamma forms; and external contour tails return to the quadratic-sum endpoint.",
